        "text": "Diagnosis:\n- All SMTP send attempts have failed for the last 20 minutes.\n- Logs show smtp-relay is failing with \"535 Authentication failed: API key revoked\".\n- secrets-agent attempted to rotate the mail/sendgrid-api-key but failed due to a permissions error (\"403 (rotation service account lacks permission)\").\n- email-worker is retrying and queue depth is rising, indicating a backlog.\n\nRemediation steps taken:\n1. Restarted secrets-agent to attempt to resolve secret rotation issues.\n2. Restarted smtp-relay and email-worker to clear any cached credentials and retry with potentially updated secrets.\n3. Checked metrics; failures persist and queue depth continues to rise.\n4. Paged the on-call engineer, as the root cause is a permissions issue preventing secret rotation and automated remediation is not possible.\n\nSummary: The SMTP API key was revoked and secrets-agent cannot rotate in a new key due to permissions errors. Automated restarts did not resolve the issue. Manual intervention is required to restore secret rotation and update the SMTP API key. The on-call engineer has been paged.",
